  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The player chose to mulligan a 7-card hand that had 2 Plains, multiple white creatures including a 1-drop (Infantry Veteran), a 2-drop (Daybreak Charger), a combat trick (Moment of Triumph), and powerful late-game cards (Blessed Sanctuary, Knight of the Tusk). While the hand only has 2 lands, both are Plains which cast all the early plays. This is a keepable hand - it has a strong curve if it draws a third land, and even without one it can deploy Infantry Veteran turn 1 and Daybreak Charger turn 2. Mulliganing to 6 loses a card for no good reason.",
      "action_taken": "Mulliganed a 7-card hand with 2 Plains, a 1-drop, a 2-drop, a combat trick, and strong late-game cards.",
      "better_line": "Keep the 7-card hand. It has a playable curve starting turn 1 with Infantry Veteran, turn 2 Daybreak Charger, and just needs to draw one more land for the mid-game plays. Two lands with low-curve spells is a reasonable keep.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "Sonnet Trash",
      "decision_index": 1,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Forest turn 1 instead of Treetop Village. Since there's nothing to cast turn 1 and Treetop Village enters tapped, playing it now costs nothing while saving a future turn's tempo. The player has no 1-mana plays, so the tapped land is free on turn 1.",
      "action_taken": "Played Forest on turn 1",
      "better_line": "Play Treetop Village turn 1 (enters tapped for free since no T1 plays), then Swamp turn 2 for Oathsworn Vampire, Forest turn 3 for Uktabi Orangutan.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 5,
      "player": "GPT5n Perfect",
      "decision_index": 4,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Forest instead of Swamp means GPT5n Perfect cannot cast anything this turn. Playing Swamp would give Forest + Swamp = {1}{B}, allowing Oathsworn Vampire to be cast this turn as a 2/2 creature. Missing a turn of development when the opponent also has limited board presence.",
      "action_taken": "Played Forest, leaving no castable spells this turn.",
      "better_line": "Play Swamp, then cast Oathsworn Vampire ({1}{B}) to develop the board. Oathsworn Vampire enters tapped so it wouldn't block anyway, but getting it down a turn earlier is meaningful tempo.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 19,
      "player": "GPT5n Perfect",
      "decision_index": 7,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Chose Oathsworn Vampire (enters tapped, 2/2) over Uktabi Orangutan (2/2, enters untapped and can block immediately). The remaining 2 mana from casting Vampire has no useful purpose this turn since there's nothing in hand that costs 2 or less. Orangutan's ETB is wasted (no artifacts), but the untapped body is more immediately useful for blocking. Vampire's graveyard recursion is long-term upside, but playing the Orangutan now and saving the Vampire for a turn where its recursion or the tap drawback matters less could be better.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Oathsworn Vampire, leaving 2 mana unused with no way to spend it",
      "better_line": "Cast Uktabi Orangutan as the 2/2 that enters untapped and can immediately block, saving Oathsworn Vampire for later when its graveyard recursion is relevant",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 39,
      "player": "GPT5n Perfect",
      "decision_index": 12,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to attack with Angelic Cub 1/1 when the opponent had no untapped creatures to block and no mana available. This was a free point of damage with zero risk.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and did not declare any attackers.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Angelic Cub for 1 free damage, then play Plains and cast Taranika, Akroan Veteran in the post-combat main phase.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 54,
      "player": "Sonnet Trash",
      "decision_index": 15,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Played Forest instead of Treetop Village. Both allow casting Uktabi Orangutan this turn (2 Forest + 1 Swamp = 3 mana including G), but Treetop Village provides a creature-land for future turns, which is strictly more valuable than a basic Forest.",
      "action_taken": "Played Forest as the land drop",
